# Replace CXformIntersect2Join. Four-symbol SetOp bindings preserve each
# input's ordered columns; PredicateNullSafeEq constructs positional IS NOT
# DISTINCT FROM comparisons, and the outer Proj* restores set multiplicity.
# WeTune ProveDslRule: EQ, SQLSOLVER, verified 2026-09-05.
Intersect*<a0 s0 a1 a2>(Input<t0>,Input<t1>)|Proj*<a5 s1>(InnerJoin<p0 a3 a4>(Input<t2>,Input<t3>))|AttrsSub(a1,t0);AttrsSub(a2,t1);TableEq(t2,t0);TableEq(t3,t1);AttrsEq(a3,a1);AttrsEq(a4,a2);AttrsEq(a5,a1);SchemaEq(s1,s0);PredicateNullSafeEq(p0,a3,a4)

# Replace CXformDifference2LeftAntiSemiJoin with the anti-existence sibling of
