# Replaces CXformLeftAntiSemiApply2LeftAntiSemiJoinNoCorrelations. AntiApply
# binds the exact inner-to-outer dependency set; AttrsEmpty is therefore the
# native promise expressed as data. AntiJoin is ordinary NOT EXISTS semantics,
# distinct from the NULL-aware AntiJoinNotIn family. This exact RuleIR is
# accepted by the FormalSQL/Rocq kernel.
AntiApply<p0 a0 a1 a2>(Input<t0>,Input<t1>)|AntiJoin<p1 a3 a4>(Input<t2>,Input<t3>)|TableEq(t2,t0);TableEq(t3,t1);PredicateEq(p1,p0);AttrsEq(a3,a0);AttrsEq(a4,a1);AttrsEmpty(a2);AttrsSub(a0,t0);AttrsSub(a1,t1);ErrorFree(p0);ErrorFree(p1)

# Replaces CXformLeftAntiSemiApplyNotIn2LeftAntiSemiJoinNotInNoCorrelations.
# AntiApplyNotIn and AntiJoinNotIn are first-class NULL-aware operators rather
# than aliases of ordinary anti semantics. Their predicate denotes the
# user-visible ALL comparison; the ORCA adapter alone handles the inverse
# comparison stored by its physical operator representation. AttrsEmpty is the
# native xform's complete uncorrelated applicability domain. This exact RuleIR
# was proved EQ by SQLSolver on 2026-08-31.
AntiApplyNotIn<p0 a0 a1 a2>(Input<t0>,Input<t1>)|AntiJoinNotIn<p1 a3 a4>(Input<t2>,Input<t3>)|TableEq(t2,t0);TableEq(t3,t1);PredicateEq(p1,p0);AttrsEq(a3,a0);AttrsEq(a4,a1);AttrsEmpty(a2);AttrsSub(a0,t0);AttrsSub(a1,t1)

# Replaces the single correlated-Filter decorrelation domain of
# CXformLeftAntiSemiApplyNotIn2LeftAntiSemiJoinNotIn. The first target predicate
# is the user-visible ALL comparison; the second is the RHS qualification that
# selects which inner rows participate. The adapter emits ORCA's equivalent raw
# predicate, inverse(comparison) AND qualification, without conflating the two
# dependency domains. This exact RuleIR was proved EQ by SQLSolver on
# 2026-08-31.
AntiApplyNotIn<p0 a0 a1 a2>(Input<t0>,Filter<p1 a3 a4>(Input<t1>))|AntiJoinNotIn<p2 a5 a6 p3 a7 a8>(Input<t2>,Input<t3>)|TableEq(t2,t0);TableEq(t3,t1);PredicateEq(p2,p0);AttrsEq(a5,a0);AttrsEq(a6,a1);PredicateEq(p3,p1);AttrsEq(a7,a4);AttrsEq(a8,a3);AttrsEq(a2,a4);AttrsSub(a0,t0);AttrsSub(a1,t1);AttrsSub(a3,t1);AttrsSub(a4,t0)

# Extends the NULL-aware decorrelation domain across a grouped aggregate when
# its correlation key is not already grouped. AttrsUnion/SchemaUnion construct
# the compensated aggregate, CorrelationEquality validates an exact conjunction
# of cross-input equality edges. AttrsNonEmpty, the ordered group/schema
# constructors, and scalar safety compose the operator-local movement law.
# PredicateEq preserves the complete
# three-valued ALL scalar tree independently of the RHS qualifier.
# This exact RuleIR was accepted by the FormalSQL/Rocq kernel on 2026-08-31.
AntiApplyNotIn<p0 a0 a1 a2>(Input<t0>,Agg<a3 a4 f0 s0 p1>(Filter<p2 a5 a6>(Input<t1>)))|AntiJoinNotIn<p3 a7 a8 p4 a9 a10>(Input<t2>,Agg<a11 a12 f1 s1 p5>(Input<t3>))|TableEq(t2,t0);TableEq(t3,t1);PredicateEq(p3,p0);AttrsEq(a7,a0);AttrsEq(a8,a1);PredicateEq(p4,p2);AttrsEq(a9,a6);AttrsEq(a10,a5);AttrsEq(a2,a6);AttrsUnion(a11,a3,a5);AttrsEq(a12,a4);FuncEq(f1,f0);SchemaUnion(s1,s0,a5);PredicateEq(p5,p1);CorrelationEquality(p2,a5,a6);AttrsNonEmpty(a5);AttrsSub(a0,t0);AttrsSub(a1,s0);AttrsSub(a3,t1);AttrsSub(a4,t1);AttrsSub(a5,t1);AttrsSub(a6,t0);Deterministic(p0);Deterministic(p3);Deterministic(p2);Deterministic(p4);ErrorFree(p0);ErrorFree(a4);ErrorFree(f0);ErrorFree(p1);ErrorFree(p2);ErrorFree(p3);ErrorFree(a12);ErrorFree(f1);ErrorFree(p5);ErrorFree(p4)

# Extends NULL-aware decorrelation across a cumulative Window.  The runtime
# rule composes atomic facts: equality correlation, non-empty local keys covered
# by PARTITION BY and outer-column independence for partition/order/items.
# ErrorFree(window-items) already admits only the shared aggregate whitelist,
# so no duplicate window-kind constraint is needed.
# The target keeps the exact Window metadata and moves the correlation into the
# AntiJoinNotIn qualifier.  FormalSQL/Rocq accepted this operator-local theorem
# on 2026-08-31.
AntiApplyNotIn<p0 a0 a1 a2>(Input<t0>,WindowRows<a3 o0 w0>(Filter<p1 a4 a5>(Input<t1>)))|AntiJoinNotIn<p2 a6 a7 p3 a8 a9>(Input<t2>,WindowRows<a10 o1 w1>(Input<t3>))|TableEq(t2,t0);TableEq(t3,t1);PredicateEq(p2,p0);AttrsEq(a6,a0);AttrsEq(a7,a1);PredicateEq(p3,p1);AttrsEq(a8,a5);AttrsEq(a9,a4);AttrsEq(a2,a5);AttrsEq(a10,a3);OrderEq(o1,o0);WindowEq(w1,w0);CorrelationEquality(p1,a4,a5);AttrsNonEmpty(a4);AttrsSub(a4,a3);DepsDisjoint(a3,a5);DepsDisjoint(o0,a5);DepsDisjoint(w0,a5);AttrsSub(a0,t0);AttrsSub(a4,t1);AttrsSub(a5,t0);Deterministic(p0);Deterministic(p2);Deterministic(p1);Deterministic(p3);ErrorFree(p0);ErrorFree(w0);ErrorFree(p1);ErrorFree(p2);ErrorFree(w1);ErrorFree(p3)

# The explicit-frame sibling covers ORCA's normalized representation of SQL
# default frames as well as genuine ROWS/RANGE frames.  FrameEq preserves the
# exact frame and DepsDisjoint additionally rejects outer-column references in
# frame edges.  FormalSQL/Rocq accepted the generic composed theorem
# on 2026-08-31.
AntiApplyNotIn<p0 a0 a1 a2>(Input<t0>,Window<a3 o0 m0 w0>(Filter<p1 a4 a5>(Input<t1>)))|AntiJoinNotIn<p2 a6 a7 p3 a8 a9>(Input<t2>,Window<a10 o1 m1 w1>(Input<t3>))|TableEq(t2,t0);TableEq(t3,t1);PredicateEq(p2,p0);AttrsEq(a6,a0);AttrsEq(a7,a1);PredicateEq(p3,p1);AttrsEq(a8,a5);AttrsEq(a9,a4);AttrsEq(a2,a5);AttrsEq(a10,a3);OrderEq(o1,o0);FrameEq(m1,m0);WindowEq(w1,w0);CorrelationEquality(p1,a4,a5);AttrsNonEmpty(a4);AttrsSub(a4,a3);DepsDisjoint(a3,a5);DepsDisjoint(o0,a5);DepsDisjoint(m0,a5);DepsDisjoint(w0,a5);AttrsSub(a0,t0);AttrsSub(a4,t1);AttrsSub(a5,t0);Deterministic(p0);Deterministic(p2);Deterministic(p1);Deterministic(p3);ErrorFree(p0);ErrorFree(w0);ErrorFree(p1);ErrorFree(p2);ErrorFree(w1);ErrorFree(p3)

# Pull a correlated Filter above a Window when every local correlation key is
# covered by the partition. These are operator-local rules: once the Filter is
# exposed, every Apply family reuses its existing Filter decorrelation rule by
# ordinary Cascade chaining. Both RuleIRs are accepted by FormalSQL/Rocq; no
# Apply-specific lowering is hidden in this normalization.
WindowRows<a0 o0 w0>(Filter<p0 a1 a2>(Input<t0>))|Filter<p1 a4 a5>(WindowRows<a3 o1 w1>(Input<t1>))|TableEq(t1,t0);AttrsEq(a3,a0);OrderEq(o1,o0);WindowEq(w1,w0);PredicateEq(p1,p0);AttrsEq(a4,a1);AttrsEq(a5,a2);CorrelationEquality(p0,a1,a2);AttrsNonEmpty(a1);AttrsSub(a1,a0);DepsDisjoint(a0,a2);DepsDisjoint(o0,a2);DepsDisjoint(w0,a2);Deterministic(p0);ErrorFree(p0);ErrorFree(p1);ErrorFree(w0);ErrorFree(w1)
Window<a0 o0 m0 w0>(Filter<p0 a1 a2>(Input<t0>))|Filter<p1 a4 a5>(Window<a3 o1 m1 w1>(Input<t1>))|TableEq(t1,t0);AttrsEq(a3,a0);OrderEq(o1,o0);FrameEq(m1,m0);WindowEq(w1,w0);PredicateEq(p1,p0);AttrsEq(a4,a1);AttrsEq(a5,a2);CorrelationEquality(p0,a1,a2);AttrsNonEmpty(a1);AttrsSub(a1,a0);DepsDisjoint(a0,a2);DepsDisjoint(o0,a2);DepsDisjoint(m0,a2);DepsDisjoint(w0,a2);Deterministic(p0);ErrorFree(p0);ErrorFree(p1);ErrorFree(w0);ErrorFree(w1)

# Compose that movement through an enclosing safe Compute. This remains an
# operator-local normalization over an arbitrary Input; it is not tied to an
# Apply family. FormalSQL/Rocq: OUTCOME_EQ, verified 2026-09-06.
Compute<e0 a0 s0>(WindowRows<a1 o0 w0>(Filter<p0 a2 a3>(Input<t0>)))|Filter<p1 a5 a6>(Compute<e1 a4 s1>(WindowRows<a7 o1 w1>(Input<t1>)))|TableEq(t1,t0);ExprListEq(e1,e0);AttrsEq(a4,a0);SchemaEq(s1,s0);AttrsEq(a7,a1);OrderEq(o1,o0);WindowEq(w1,w0);PredicateEq(p1,p0);AttrsEq(a5,a2);AttrsEq(a6,a3);CorrelationEquality(p0,a2,a3);AttrsNonEmpty(a2);AttrsSub(a2,a1);DepsDisjoint(a1,a3);DepsDisjoint(o0,a3);DepsDisjoint(w0,a3);DepsDisjoint(p0,s0);Deterministic(e0);ErrorFree(e0);Deterministic(p0);ErrorFree(p0);ErrorFree(w0);ErrorFree(e1);Deterministic(e1);ErrorFree(p1);ErrorFree(w1)
Compute<e0 a0 s0>(Window<a1 o0 m0 w0>(Filter<p0 a2 a3>(Input<t0>)))|Filter<p1 a5 a6>(Compute<e1 a4 s1>(Window<a7 o1 m1 w1>(Input<t1>)))|TableEq(t1,t0);ExprListEq(e1,e0);AttrsEq(a4,a0);SchemaEq(s1,s0);AttrsEq(a7,a1);OrderEq(o1,o0);FrameEq(m1,m0);WindowEq(w1,w0);PredicateEq(p1,p0);AttrsEq(a5,a2);AttrsEq(a6,a3);CorrelationEquality(p0,a2,a3);AttrsNonEmpty(a2);AttrsSub(a2,a1);DepsDisjoint(a1,a3);DepsDisjoint(o0,a3);DepsDisjoint(m0,a3);DepsDisjoint(w0,a3);DepsDisjoint(p0,s0);Deterministic(e0);ErrorFree(e0);Deterministic(p0);ErrorFree(p0);ErrorFree(w0);ErrorFree(e1);Deterministic(e1);ErrorFree(p1);ErrorFree(w1)

# A residual Filter may consume a Window result and therefore stays below the
