Compute<e0 a0 s0>(Filter<p0 a1>(Window<a2 o0 m0 w0>(Filter<p1 a3 a4>(Input<t0>))))|Filter<p2 a5 a6>(Compute<e1 a7 s1>(Filter<p3 a8>(Window<a9 o1 m1 w1>(Input<t1>))))|TableEq(t1,t0);ExprListEq(e1,e0);AttrsEq(a7,a0);SchemaEq(s1,s0);PredicateEq(p3,p0);AttrsEq(a8,a1);AttrsEq(a9,a2);OrderEq(o1,o0);FrameEq(m1,m0);WindowEq(w1,w0);PredicateEq(p2,p1);AttrsEq(a5,a3);AttrsEq(a6,a4);CorrelationEquality(p1,a3,a4);AttrsNonEmpty(a3);AttrsSub(a3,a2);DepsDisjoint(a2,a4);DepsDisjoint(o0,a4);DepsDisjoint(m0,a4);DepsDisjoint(w0,a4);DepsDisjoint(p1,s0);ErrorFree(e0);Deterministic(e0);ErrorFree(p0);Deterministic(p0);ErrorFree(p1);Deterministic(p1);ErrorFree(w0);ErrorFree(e1);Deterministic(e1);ErrorFree(p2);Deterministic(p2);ErrorFree(p3);Deterministic(p3);ErrorFree(w1)

# Replaces the single correlated-Filter decorrelation domain of
# CXformLeftSemiApply2LeftSemiJoin. AttrsUnion derives the target predicate's
# complete per-child dependencies when the Apply predicate and pulled Filter
# predicate reference different columns. This exact RuleIR is accepted by the
# generic FormalSQL/Rocq proof kernel.
SemiApply<p0 a0 a1 a2>(Input<t0>,Filter<p1 a3 a4>(Input<t1>))|SemiJoin<p2 a5 a6>(Input<t2>,Input<t3>)|TableEq(t2,t0);TableEq(t3,t1);PredicateAnd(p2,p0,p1);AttrsEq(a2,a4);AttrsUnion(a5,a0,a4);AttrsUnion(a6,a1,a3);AttrsSub(a0,t0);AttrsSub(a1,t1);AttrsSub(a3,t1);AttrsSub(a4,t0);Deterministic(p0);Deterministic(p1);Deterministic(p2);ErrorFree(p0);ErrorFree(p1);ErrorFree(p2)

# Atomic composition of the generic Window/Filter movement and SemiApply
# decorrelation laws. It is needed when Cascades cannot place the intermediate
# Window alternative in the Apply's original memo group. FormalSQL/Rocq
# accepted this RuleIR on 2026-09-05.
SemiApply<p0 a0 a1 a2>(Input<t0>,Window<a3 o0 m0 w0>(Filter<p1 a4 a5>(Input<t1>)))|SemiJoin<p2 a6 a7>(Input<t2>,Window<a8 o1 m1 w1>(Input<t3>))|TableEq(t2,t0);TableEq(t3,t1);PredicateAnd(p2,p0,p1);AttrsEq(a2,a5);AttrsUnion(a6,a0,a5);AttrsUnion(a7,a1,a4);AttrsEq(a8,a3);OrderEq(o1,o0);FrameEq(m1,m0);WindowEq(w1,w0);CorrelationEquality(p1,a4,a5);AttrsNonEmpty(a4);AttrsSub(a4,a3);DepsDisjoint(a3,a5);DepsDisjoint(o0,a5);DepsDisjoint(m0,a5);DepsDisjoint(w0,a5);AttrsSub(a0,t0);AttrsSub(a4,t1);AttrsSub(a5,t0);Deterministic(p0);Deterministic(p1);Deterministic(p2);ErrorFree(p0);ErrorFree(p1);ErrorFree(p2);ErrorFree(w0);ErrorFree(w1)

# Collapses any two adjacent correlated or ordinary Filters into one explicit
# conjunction. This is an independently Rocq-proved normalization rule, not an
# Apply-specific adapter; it lets existing one-Filter rules consume deeper
# predicate stacks through ordinary Cascade chaining.
Filter<p0 a0 a1>(Filter<p1 a2 a3>(Input<t0>))|Filter<p2 a4 a5>(Input<t1>)|TableEq(t1,t0);PredicateAnd(p2,p0,p1);AttrsUnion(a4,a0,a2);AttrsUnion(a5,a1,a3);AttrsSub(a0,t0);AttrsSub(a2,t0);Deterministic(p0);Deterministic(p1);Deterministic(p2);ErrorFree(p0);ErrorFree(p1);ErrorFree(p2)

# Replaces the single correlated-Filter decorrelation domain of
